kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "app-tui"
purpose: "跨切面不变量索引：保留旧 app-tui 中与引擎/渲染解耦的架构约束（三面共存、reuse-contract、无 skeleton spray、Driver 契约等）。产品细节 req 已迁至 app-tui-* 各能力。本 spec 将在 c450 归档后合并至各子能力或退役。"
valid_scope[2]: src/,tests/
requirements[39]{req_id,title,statement}:
  tui1,"line-array-differential-render","The TUI MUST render using a self-built differential render engine over a line-array screen representation (previous_lines vs new_lines per-frame diff, writing only changed lines wrapped in synchronized output CSI 2026), driven by crossterm directly for raw mode/events/cursor. The TUI MUST NOT use ratatui (cell-grid Buffer, immediate-mode Widget trait, Viewport::Inline, or insert_before). The engine owns the whole conversation history as a single Vec of styled lines; streaming appends new lines via diff (no irreversible commit). The viewport MUST anchor to the content tail every frame: previous_viewport_top = max(0, max(terminal_height, total_lines) - terminal_height). Evidence: pi-tui line-array + viewport anchoring (tui.ts:1318-1319 bufferLength = max(height, newLines.length)); the prior ratatui inline-viewport model forced commit-unit = render-unit = paragraph, losing cross-paragraph markdown context (the c396 screenshot root cause)."
  tui2,"in-process-driver","The TUI MUST drive the agent via app::core::driver::InProcessDriver (the same Driver path as print mode); the TUI MUST NOT default to a RemoteDriver or an auto-spawned daemon. Evidence: codex AppServerTarget::Embedded is the TUI default (codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs:814-830); pi InteractiveMode holds AgentSessionRuntime directly (coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/interactive-mode.ts:265,391)."
  tui3,"three-surfaces-coexist","The rpc (stdio JSONL), server (REST+WS), and tui (inline) application surfaces MUST coexist; none MAY be removed in the name of unification. Evidence: codex keeps in-process TUI + app-server stdio (powers VSCode ext) + app-server-daemon (unix socket); pi keeps in-process TUI + --mode rpc + orchestrator serve; neither project dropped any transport."
  tui4,"reuse-contract","The TUI MUST import only crate::agent (mod-level), crate::app::core (Driver/composition), crate::protocol, and crate::domain; it MUST NOT import crate::agent::session, crate::agent::runtime, or crate::infra. Slash command semantics MUST reuse protocol::Command variants rather than inventing a parallel command vocabulary."
  tui5,"no-skeleton-spray","Every file created under src/app/tui/ MUST be driven by a real entry point (tui::run) within its own change; the TUI MUST NOT use #[allow(dead_code)] to land undriven skeleton code. Undriven skeleton is the documented root cause of the prior two failed TUI attempts."
  tui10,"repl-entry","The CLI MUST dispatch to app::tui::run when no prompt is provided and stdin is a TTY (mirroring pi resolveAppMode), entering an inline REPL driven by InProcessDriver; a --tui flag MAY force the TUI even with a prompt."
  tui11,"event-loop","The TUI MUST run a tokio::select! event loop multiplexing three sources: the XyEvent stream from Driver::run, crossterm keyboard input via EventStream (requires crossterm event-stream feature), and a cancellation signal that calls Driver::abort."
  tui12,"line-array-render-pipeline","The TUI MUST render via a per-frame pipeline: widget tree render(width) produces a flat Vec of StyledLine (the whole conversation), the engine diffs against previous_lines by line equality, picks one of three strategies (first render without clearing, full redraw with clearing, normal diff with line clear + rewrite), wraps writes in synchronized output, positions a virtual IME cursor, and saves state. The hard width invariant MUST fire on both the diff path AND the full-redraw path (an over-wide line is a hard error, not silent wrap). At save-state, previous_viewport_top MUST be set to max(0, max(terminal_height, total_lines) - terminal_height) centrally in do_render, not in each strategy branch, ensuring the viewport always follows the content tail regardless of the render path taken."
  tui13,"xyevent-coverage","The TUI render MUST handle at minimum these XyEvent variants: TextDelta (stream to tail then commit on boundary), ThinkingDelta, ToolExecutionStart/Update/End, ModelSelect, Error, TurnStart/TurnEnd; unhandled variants MUST degrade gracefully (e.g. log) not panic."
  tui14,"slash-commands","The TUI MUST parse slash commands /exit (maps to Quit) and /model (maps to SetModel or CycleModel) reusing protocol::Command semantics; unknown slash input MUST show an inline error not crash."
  tui15,"terminal-lifecycle","The TUI MUST enable raw mode and Viewport::Inline on entry and MUST restore the terminal on exit via Drop or explicit teardown even on panic or error, so the user's terminal is never left in a broken raw-mode state."
  tui20,"core-backend-direct","The TUI MUST depend on ratatui-core and ratatui-crossterm directly (NOT the umbrella ratatui crate); the umbrella ratatui dependency MUST be removed from Cargo.toml. Evidence: ratatui-core v0.1.2 contains all types used (Terminal/Frame/Viewport::Inline/insert_before/set_cursor_position/Buffer/Layout/Style/Text/Line/Span/Widget trait) at ratatui/ratatui-core/src/; umbrella init.rs convenience (try_init_with_options/restore/DefaultTerminal) is ~15 lines replicated locally. ratatui-crossterm provides CrosstermBackend (ratatui/ratatui-crossterm/src/lib.rs:160)."
  tui21,"widget-usage-policy","The TUI MUST NOT be constrained to hand-rolled cell loops: ratatui-widgets (the independent crate, NOT the umbrella ratatui) is an allowed dependency, and its subset (Paragraph/Block/List/ListState/Clear) MAY be reused when it fits. When a library widget does not meet the inline-rendering need (e.g. a specific CJK/emoji behavior, or a custom interaction), the TUI MAY instead build a self-contained widget on top of ratatui-core primitives (Buffer/Layout/Style/Text/Widget trait). The umbrella ratatui crate MUST remain absent (see tui20). The choice between reuse and self-build MUST be driven by fit, not by a blanket prohibition."
  tui22,"scrolling-regions","The TUI MUST enable the ratatui-core scrolling-regions feature (forwarded via ratatui-crossterm) to reduce insert_before flicker; this addresses the c340 §7 known-leftover insert_before jelly effect."
  tui30,"user-message-echo","The TUI MUST commit the user's submitted prompt text to the scrollback immediately on Enter (before or during driver.run), styled distinctly (e.g. ❯ prefix) so the user sees their own message in the conversation history. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #3 noted user input never reached scrollback; pi/kimi-code user-message components (kimi-code/apps/kimi-code/src/tui/components/messages/user-message.ts) echo user input on submit."
  tui31,"turn-end-flush-consistent","The TUI MUST flush the final streaming line to scrollback and clear the tail in the same frame on TurnEnd, so no reply text lingers in the mutable tail after a turn completes. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #4 noted the last reply line stayed in the tail until the next submit."
  tui32,"input-anchored-visual","The TUI input region MUST appear visually at the bottom of the terminal (no floating/gap错觉); the loader status line MUST appear immediately above the input region, also at the visible bottom. When the conversation history exceeds the terminal height, the viewport MUST scroll such that the bottom rows (loader + input) remain in the last visible screen positions, and earlier content scrolls above the viewport. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #1 noted Viewport::Inline(3) left a perceived gap; pi achieves bottom anchoring via viewport_top = max(0, max(height, lines.length) - height) without any special footer region."
  tui40,"panic-hook-restore","The TUI MUST install a std::panic::set_hook before entering the inline viewport that restores the terminal (disable raw mode + restore) before chaining to the original hook, so the terminal is never left broken even under panic=abort or when a panic occurs in a spawned task whose stack has no InlineTerminal. Drop alone is insufficient: it does not run under panic=abort, and a panic in a spawn_blocking/spawn child task unwinds that child's stack (no InlineTerminal there). Evidence: codex tui.rs installs a panic hook for terminal restore; Rust's set_hook still executes under panic=abort whereas Drop does not."
  tui41,"virtual-terminal-test-harness","The TUI rendering layer MUST be covered by an in-memory virtual terminal cell-grid harness (feed the engine's ANSI output stream, assert on cell content, cursor position, and styles per row), covering at minimum: the per-frame diff path (append-only growth, in-place edit, width change full redraw, shrink orphan-row clearing), streaming text wrapping at terminal width (CJK-aware), and clean exit. This replaces the prior ratatui TestBackend harness (which asserted on ratatui Buffer cells and is unavailable once ratatui is removed). Evidence: skill terminal-foundations.md testing-strategy (headless terminal emulator as VirtualTerminal); pi-tui uses @xterm/headless."
  tui42,"render-business-decoupling","The TUI rendering layer MUST be decoupled from the agent data/business flow: rendering functions MUST consume UI-only data types (e.g. a RenderedLine enum: UserInput/AssistantText/ToolSummary/Status) rather than domain XyEvent variants directly. The boundary between the UI/UX layer and the data-flow/business-flow layer MUST be explicit: business events (XyEvent) are translated into UI data types at a single seam, and the rendering layer MUST NOT match on XyEvent variants or call Driver/agent methods. Evidence: the current render::commit_lines_for (src/app/tui/render.rs:119) and app::handle_xy_event (src/app/tui/app.rs:102) mix XyEvent handling with line production, coupling rendering to the domain event vocabulary; codex isolates via HistoryCell (codex-rs/tui/src/history_cell/) and pi via typed message parts (packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/assistant-message.ts)."
  tui50,"streaming-via-line-array-append","The TUI streaming render MUST grow the in-progress assistant text by appending new rendered lines to the line-array (the engine diffs and writes only the new lines, scrolling the viewport to follow the end). The mutable region and the scrollback are a single unified line-array (no two-region split, no irreversible commit). The whole accumulated turn source is re-rendered each frame so cross-paragraph markdown context (block blank-line spacing, list/blockquote prefix continuity) is preserved. TurnEnd flushes the residual tail (already in the line-array; just marks streaming done). Evidence: skill rendering-engine.md Step 5 normal diff append case; the prior two-region (mutable last line + irreversible insert_before scrollback) model forced the c377 fence-aware paragraph hack and lost cross-paragraph context."
  tui51,"render-layer-componentized","The TUI rendering layer MUST be decomposed into reusable, self-contained widgets under the tui components directory, each consuming only UI-only data types (RenderedLine, a string, spinner index, input buffer), each independently verifiable via a TestBackend, and each composable by a layout widget (Tail) that bottom-anchors its children. At minimum: TranscriptLine (RenderedLine into Buffer for the insert_before commit path), MutableLine (pending tail at tail buffer top, wrapped, transparent bg), ThinkingIndicator (spinner plus label), InputPrompt (prompt plus input plus cursor plus input_bg block, CJK-aware cursor), Tail (composes the above, bottom-anchored, capacity-aware top-drop). draw_tail_frame MUST delegate to Tail render; commit_to_scrollback MUST consume a slice of RenderedLine and render via TranscriptLine. The rendering layer MUST NOT use direct terminal escape-sequence writes (raw escape or DECSTBM scroll-region manipulation) that bypass the ratatui buffer — such code is not widget-able (bound to physical coordinates), not TestBackend-verifiable (violates tui41), and bypasses the RenderedLine seam (violates tui42). Evidence: user goal that every TUI part be an explainable, reusable, individually-verifiable widget (component); the escape route (raw_render.rs) was the one non-widget-able part and produced the reply-cleared bug."
  tui52,"multi-round-turn-not-truncated","The TUI MUST drain the agent XyEvent stream for a user prompt until the stream ends (returns None) and MUST NOT stop at the first XyEvent::TurnEnd. The react loop emits one TurnEnd per ReAct iteration; a tool-calling turn spans multiple iterations (the model calls a tool then continues in a later iteration) so intermediate TurnEnds are single-iteration boundaries not the end of the whole user turn. The turn-fully-done signal (when to clear the mutable tail and reset streaming state) MUST be stream termination (None) delivered as an explicit end-of-stream message to the main loop, NOT a mid-stream TurnEnd. Evidence: spawn_drain broke on the first TurnEnd so tool-calling turns had their continuation events dropped and the REPL appeared to hang after a tool call; print mode consumes the whole stream via while-let-Some and is unaffected, confirming the multi-TurnEnd protocol is by design and the bug is TUI-side."
  tui53,"always-on-status-line","The TUI MUST render a status line between the conversation history and the input panel, occupying exactly one row every frame (idle and streaming). The status line MUST appear at the second-to-last visible row (immediately above the input) regardless of conversation length—the viewport MUST shift upward as content grows to keep the status line + input in the visible bottom. The status line shows a spinner glyph (animated by the existing Tick-driven loader) followed by a single left-aligned activity label: Working while streaming with no tool, Running {tool} while a tool executes, Ready while idle. The status line MUST NOT show a turn count or model name."
  tui60,"markdown-render-component","The TUI MUST provide a MarkdownRenderer component (src/app/tui/components/markdown.rs) that consumes a finalized string plus a MarkdownStyle and produces Vec<Line> for the ratatui buffer; RenderedLine::UserInput and RenderedLine::AssistantText MUST both render through this shared MarkdownRenderer, differing only in the injected MarkdownStyle (user_prompt palette vs assistant palette), so user input and LLM replies share identical structural rendering. The renderer MUST be backed by pulldown-cmark (not a hand-written parser). Evidence: codex uses pulldown-cmark + syntect (markdown_render.rs:825-863); pi uses marked.lexer + MarkdownTheme function injection with user/assistant sharing one Markdown class (assistant-message.ts:103 vs user-message.ts:31); kimi-code reuses pi-tui Markdown."
  tui61,"markdown-scope-full-graded-headings","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render at minimum: graded headings (H1 bold+underlined, H2 bold, H3 bold+italic, H4-H6 italic, each with a leading hash-repeat prefix matching its level), bold/code inline, fenced code blocks (with syntect highlighting, no background/border/language-label), unordered lists (bullet marker), ordered lists (auto-incrementing number marker colored light_blue), task lists, blockquotes (with a visible greater-than prefix on every physical row), tables (aligned columns, no border lines), and CJK-aware paragraph wrapping. Syntax highlighting of fenced code blocks is provided by a syntect backend (tui70/tui71); OSC8 hyperlinks and streaming incremental markdown parsing remain excluded. Streaming text in the mutable last line stays plain text; markdown rendering applies only after a line is finalized and committed to scrollback."
  tui65,"thinking-text-via-markdown","The TUI MUST render finalized ThinkingText through the shared MarkdownRenderer (same as UserInput/AssistantText since c355), via a dedicated MarkdownStyle (for_thinking) that preserves the dim/italic visual hierarchy of reasoning content while still parsing code blocks, lists, and inline formatting. The streaming mutable thinking line stays plain text (spec tui61 streaming-stays-plain still holds); markdown rendering applies only after a thinking line is finalized and committed to scrollback. Evidence: codex AgentMarkdownCell does not distinguish thinking vs text in markdown parsing (only styling); pi shares one Markdown class across thinking/assistant with style parameters; current render.rs:81 ThinkingText branch bypasses render_markdown entirely."
  tui66,"blockquote-visual-prefix-gt","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render blockquote lines with a visible leading prefix of the greater-than character followed by a space colored with the quote style, so blockquotes are distinguishable from plain paragraph text on terminals where the dim color difference is hard to perceive. The prefix MUST appear on every physical row of the blockquote (including wrapped continuation rows), and MUST indent for nested blockquotes (each nesting level adds another greater-than, so a double-nested quote renders with a doubled prefix). Evidence: codex uses a vertical-bar left border for blockquotes; pi keeps the greater-than prefix; the c355 blockquote renderer applied only dim style with no glyph, which was visually indistinguishable from normal text."
  tui70,"self-research-markdown-line-array","The TUI markdown rendering MUST be backed by the self-researched lightweight renderer (pulldown-cmark + syntect, no box-drawing borders/tree-connectors/table-lines), producing the engine's native StyledLine type (not ratatui Line) so it integrates directly into the line-array diff. Code blocks use syntect highlighting without background/border/language-label. The MarkdownStyle adapter (for_user/for_assistant/for_thinking) remains the single seam. Tables render as tab/space-aligned plain text (no Unicode border characters) so copy-paste yields clean low-token markdown. Evidence: skill ui-components.md Markdown widget + D6 token-economy principle; c395/c396 styling carries over (heading grading, blockquote greater-than prefix, ordered-list number marker)."
  tui71,"code-highlight-theme-adaptive","The TUI code block syntax highlighting (via syntect + two-face, default-fancy pure-Rust backend) MUST highlight fenced code blocks in recognized languages using a theme adapted to the terminal background lightness, and MUST fall back to plain unstyled text when the language is unrecognized OR the input exceeds safety limits (512 KB / 10000 lines), so rendering never blocks or panics on pathological input. Theme selection MUST pick a light theme (CatppuccinLatte) when the COLORFGBS environment variable indicates a light background (background code >= 7), and a dark theme (CatppuccinMocha) otherwise (including when COLORFGBS is unset). The selected theme MUST be cached for the process lifetime."
  tui72,"link-renders-copyable-url","The TUI markdown renderer MUST render inline links in a copyable form: a [text](url) link MUST render as the link text followed by the full URL in parentheses (text (url)), and an angle-bracket autolink MUST render as the bare URL, so users can see and manually select-copy the URL in terminals where OSC8 clickable links are unsupported. The URL MUST be visually distinct (primary color plus underline); the wrapping parentheses MUST be dimmed. Empty link text MUST render just the URL."
  tui75,"stream-incremental-highlight","The TUI MUST render streaming assistant text incrementally: each TextDelta triggers a full re-render of the accumulated turn source via render_markdown, lines up to the last newline boundary (stable) are committed to scrollback WITH syntax highlighting, and the unstable tail stays in the mutable region (also highlighted, not plain text). This gives streaming-time line-by-line scrollback updates with full markdown/highlight context, unlike deferred-commit which blocks until TurnEnd. Code blocks render highlighted even with unclosed fences (verified: vendored parser tolerates unclosed fences)."
  tui76,"input-cursor-horizontal","The TUI input line MUST support horizontal cursor movement: Left/Right arrows move the cursor by one character (CJK-aware boundary), Home/End jump to start/end. Characters are inserted at the cursor position (not always appended at the end); Backspace deletes the character before the cursor. The rendered cursor column reflects the display width of the text before the cursor (not the whole buffer)."
  tui77,"fence-aware-paragraph-commit","The TUI streaming text commit MUST be fence-aware: outside a fenced code block, text commits at paragraph boundaries (blank lines); inside a fenced code block (opened by triple-backtick), all lines accumulate until the closing fence, then the complete code block commits as a single unit. This ensures render_markdown receives complete fence context so syntax highlighting applies during streaming (not deferred to TurnEnd). Blank lines inside a code block do NOT split the block."
  tui78,"heading-graded-by-level","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render headings with level-graded styling: H1 MUST be bold plus underlined, H2 MUST be bold, H3 MUST be bold plus italic, and H4/H5/H6 MUST be italic. Each heading MUST carry a leading prefix of N hash characters followed by a space matching its level (so a level-1 heading renders with a single hash prefix, level-2 with a double hash prefix, etc). Evidence: codex MarkdownStyles assigns distinct styles per level and start_heading prepends the hash prefix (codex-rs/tui/src/markdown_render.rs:89-105 and 579-580); the c395 renderer applied a single bold style to all levels and dropped the prefix, flattening the document outline."
  tui79,"ordered-list-number-marker","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render ordered list items with an auto-incrementing number marker (e.g. 1. 2. 3.) colored light_blue, incrementing from the list start value across sibling items. Unordered list items MUST render with a bullet marker. Evidence: codex start_item emits an index-followed-by-dot marker in ordered_list_marker style (codex-rs/tui/src/markdown_render.rs:772-799); the c395 renderer dropped the ordered-list start tag into a catch-all no-op, losing the number marker entirely."
  tui82,"engine-width-contract","The TUI differential render engine MUST enforce a hard width contract: every StyledLine produced by a widget MUST have display width less than or equal to the render width, checked on BOTH the normal-diff write path AND the full-redraw path. An over-wide line MUST abort with a diagnostic (width, offending line, crash log) rather than silently wrapping and desyncing every subsequent diff row. Width utilities MUST be ANSI-aware (SGR/OSC sequences count zero width) and wide-char-aware (CJK/emoji count width 2, combining marks count 0). Evidence: skill rendering-engine.md Step 6 + audit.md Finding 2 (pi-tui only checks the diff path; the port must check both)."
  tui83,"engine-resize-adaptive","The TUI MUST handle terminal resize (window size change AND font zoom changing rows/columns) by treating any width change as a full redraw (wrapping changes every line) and any height change as a full redraw (to keep the viewport aligned), rebuilding the widget tree at the new width and re-diffing. Resize MUST NOT lose content, lose the input cursor, corrupt the streaming state, or leave orphan characters at line ends. The Event::Resize from crossterm MUST trigger a render frame (not be ignored). Evidence: skill rendering-engine.md Step 5B full redraw on width/height change + Step 8 viewport math; the prior model ignored Event::Resize (mod.rs let Event::Key(_) = ev else continue dropped it) and could not re-wrap committed scrollback."
  tui84,"viewport-anchoring-single-point","The engine MUST set previous_viewport_top at a single point in do_render (after all strategy branches complete), using the formula max(0, max(terminal_height, total_lines) - terminal_height). Neither diff_render nor full_render MUST modify previous_viewport_top. The anchor formula MUST use max(terminal_height, total_lines) as the working buffer size (pi bufferLength) rather than just total_lines, so short content does not create a transient non-zero viewport offset that causes the footer to drift when content subsequently grows."
scenarios[63]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui1,"viewport-anchors-to-tail",content is 15 rows and terminal height is 10,do_render saves state,"previous_viewport_top = 5 (15-10) and scrolling the terminal back shows rows 0-4 in scrollback and rows 5-14 visible"
  tui1,"short-content-anchors-to-zero",content is 3 rows and terminal height is 10,do_render saves state,previous_viewport_top = 0 and all 3 rows plus padding empty rows are visible
  tui1,"viewport-consistent-across-strategies",content grows from 5 to 15 rows across multiple frames,each frame renders via the appropriate strategy (diff or fullRender),"previous_viewport_top is consistently max(0, max(height, n) - height) regardless of which strategy was used"
  tui2,"inprocess-default",xylitol is launched with no prompt and stdin is a TTY,the TUI starts,the agent is driven via InProcessDriver not RemoteDriver
  tui3,"rpc-retained",the rpc surface is inspected after the TUI lands,"--rpc dispatch and src/app/rpc.rs are checked",rpc mode is still present and functional
  tui3,"server-retained",the server surface is inspected after the TUI lands,xylitol server run and src/app/server are checked,the server is still present and functional
  tui4,"no-infra-import",the TUI source is inspected,imports under src/app/tui are checked,"none import crate::agent::session crate::agent::runtime or crate::infra and slash commands map to protocol::Command"
  tui5,"driven-on-land",a file is added under src/app/tui,it is checked at change completion,"it is reachable from tui::run and has no #[allow(dead_code)]"
  tui10,"tty-default",xylitol is run with no arguments and stdin is a TTY,the process starts,"app::tui::run is entered and an inline REPL is shown"
  tui10,"prompt-stays-print",xylitol 'fix the bug' is run,the process starts,print mode runs (not the TUI) because a prompt was given
  tui11,"abort-on-cancel",a long agent turn is streaming,the user presses the cancel key,"Driver::abort is called and the loop breaks cleanly"
  tui12,"viewport-set-in-do-render-only",the engine source is inspected,previous_viewport_top assignment sites are checked,only do_render sets it; diff_render and full_render do not
  tui13,"textdelta-stream",a TextDelta event arrives,the tail is redrawn,the partial text is visible in the tail region and on a newline boundary is committed to scrollback
  tui13,"tool-status",a ToolExecutionStart then ToolExecutionEnd occur,the events are rendered,tool name and result preview appear without panicking
  tui14,"exit-command",the user types /exit,the command is parsed,the REPL exits cleanly restoring the terminal
  tui14,"model-command",the user types /model,the user types /model,"the model is switched via protocol::Command SetModel/CycleModel semantics"
  tui15,"restore-on-panic",the TUI panics during a turn,the panic unwinds,raw mode is disabled and the terminal is usable
  tui20,"no-umbrella-dep",Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock are inspected after the change,dependency names are checked,"ratatui 0.30.x is absent and ratatui-core + ratatui-crossterm are present"
  tui21,"widget-choice-driven-by-fit",a TUI rendering path needs to display wrapped text or a bordered box,the implementation is chosen,"either a ratatui-widgets subset (Paragraph/Block) is reused OR a self-contained widget is built on ratatui-core primitives and neither choice is blocked by a blanket prohibition"
  tui21,"umbrella-still-absent",Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock are inspected after the change,dependency names are checked,"the umbrella ratatui crate is absent while ratatui-core and ratatui-crossterm remain (and ratatui-widgets may be present)"
  tui22,"flicker-reduced",a long streaming turn with frequent TextDelta newlines is rendered in the TUI,the terminal is observed,"insert_before commits do not produce visible clear-and-redraw jelly effect (scrolling-regions engaged)"
  tui30,"user-input-visible",the user types a prompt and presses Enter,the scrollback is inspected,the user's prompt text appears as a committed line above the live tail region
  tui31,"no-tail-linger",a streaming turn reaches TurnEnd,the frame after TurnEnd is rendered,the tail contains no leftover assistant text from the finished turn and the final line is in scrollback
  tui32,"footer-visible-when-content-overflows",a ScrollbackTerminal with height=10 renders 15 rows of content (13 history + 1 loader + 1 input),the engine renders a frame,"screen rows 8 and 9 (last two) contain the loader and input lines, and no history line overlaps them"
  tui32,"footer-stays-bottom-during-growth",content grows from 8 rows to 14 rows over 6 frames,each frame is rendered,"the loader and input rows are always in the last two screen rows, and the scrollback buffer grows correctly"
  tui40,"panic-hook-installed-before-viewport",the TUI source is inspected,the run() entry point is read,"install_terminal_restore_hook is called before InlineTerminal::enter"
  tui40,"panic-abort-still-restores",the process is built with panic=abort and the TUI panics during a turn,the panic hook fires,raw mode is disabled and the terminal is usable before the process terminates
  tui41,"virtual-terminal-covers-diff","the engine is fed an append-only sequence then an in-place edit then a width change via the virtual terminal harness","the harness cell-grid is asserted","each case produces the expected cells (only new line on append, only changed line on in-place edit, full rewrite on width change) and the cursor ends at the expected position"
  tui42,"no-xyevent-in-render",the TUI rendering functions are inspected,their input types are checked,"they consume UI-only data types (e.g. RenderedLine) and no rendering function matches on XyEvent variants or calls Driver/agent methods"
  tui50,"streaming-preserves-cross-paragraph-context",an assistant reply containing a paragraph followed by a fenced code block is streamed one delta at a time,the engine renders frames during streaming,"the blank-line spacing between the paragraph and the code block renders correctly (the renderer saw the full document via per-frame full-source render) without a paragraph-split hack"
  tui51,"widgets-independently-testable",each widget under the tui components directory is exercised,it is rendered to a TestBackend buffer and asserted,"TranscriptLine, MutableLine, ThinkingIndicator, InputPrompt, Tail each render their expected content independently without a real terminal"
  tui51,"no-escape-direct-write","the tui source is inspected for escape-sequence rendering","raw_render.rs and any DECSTBM or MoveTo-then-Print bypass of the ratatui buffer are checked","no escape-sequence direct-write rendering path exists; all rendering goes through the ratatui buffer"
  tui52,"tool-turn-continuation-reaches-tui",a turn runs a tool call then the model produces a final text reply across multiple ReAct iterations,the XyEvent stream is drained by the TUI and rendered,the final text reply after the tool call is rendered in the TUI (not dropped) and the mutable tail reflects the continuation
  tui52,"drain-breaks-on-stream-end",the TUI drain task is inspected,the stream consumption loop is read,the loop breaks on stream None or external cancellation and does NOT break on an intermediate TurnEnd
  tui52,"tail-cleared-on-stream-end","a multi-iteration tool-calling turn finishes",the stream returns None,the mutable tail is cleared and streaming state is reset exactly once when the stream ends (not on the intermediate TurnEnd that precedes the continuation round)
  tui53,"status-line-second-to-last",content is 12 rows (10 history + 1 status + 1 input) with terminal height=8,the engine renders a frame,the status line is in screen row 6 and the input line is in screen row 7
  tui53,"status-line-visible-in-idle",an idle TUI with empty conversation but greeting + loader + input visible,the ScrollbackTerminal frame is inspected,"the loader row (second-to-last) shows 'Ready' and the input row (last) shows the prompt cursor"
  tui60,"user-assistant-shared-renderer",the TUI rendering source is inspected,"RenderedLine::UserInput and AssistantText rendering paths are checked","both call MarkdownRenderer with different MarkdownStyle (user_prompt vs assistant palette), not two separate rendering implementations"
  tui60,"code-block-structured",an assistant reply containing a fenced code block with language tag,the reply is finalized and committed to scrollback,"the code block renders with a language label and distinct background color (structure visible), even though syntax highlighting is not applied"
  tui61,"graded-heading-prefix-visible",an assistant reply containing headings of multiple levels is finalized and rendered via TestBackend,the buffer is inspected,"each heading row carries a hash prefix matching its level (single hash for H1, double hash for H2, etc)"
  tui65,"thinking-renders-markdown",a finalized ThinkingText line containing a fenced code block is committed to scrollback,the line is rendered,"the code block renders with language label and structure (markdown parsed), styled dim/italic to distinguish from the main reply, verified via TestBackend"
  tui65,"thinking-source-shares-renderer",the RenderedLine source is inspected,the ThinkingText rendering path is read,"it calls MarkdownRenderer via to_lines (not to_line plain), differing from AssistantText only in the injected MarkdownStyle"
  tui66,"blockquote-has-gt-prefix",an assistant reply containing a blockquote is finalized and rendered via TestBackend,the buffer is inspected,"each row of the blockquote carries a leading greater-than-space prefix colored with the quote style, present on wrapped continuation rows too"
  tui66,"nested-blockquote-gt-indents",a nested blockquote is rendered via TestBackend,the buffer is inspected,"the inner blockquote rows carry an additional greater-than so nesting is visually expressed as a doubled prefix"
  tui70,"markdown-table-copyable","an assistant reply containing a GFM table is rendered and the terminal is selected-and-copied",the copied text is inspected,"the table is tab or space aligned plain text without Unicode border characters so the copy is clean low-token markdown"
  tui71,"light-theme-when-colorfgbs-light",the COLORFGBS environment variable is set to a value indicating a light background (e.g. 0;15) and a fenced rs code block is rendered,the highlight theme is selected and the buffer cell styles are inspected,code spans use the light theme (CatppuccinLatte) palette distinct from the dark default
  tui71,"dark-theme-when-colorfgbs-unset",the COLORFGBS environment variable is unset and a fenced rs code block is rendered,the highlight theme is selected,code spans use the dark theme (CatppuccinMocha) matching the prior fixed behavior
  tui72,"inline-link-shows-url","an assistant reply containing a text-plus-url link is rendered via TestBackend",the buffer is inspected,"both the link text and the full URL are visible (URL in parentheses, suitable for manual copy)"
  tui72,"autolink-renders-bare-url","a reply containing an angle-bracket autolink is rendered via TestBackend",the buffer is inspected,the URL renders without angle brackets and is copyable
  tui75,"stream-lines-commit-with-highlight",TextDelta events stream a fenced code block line by line,each newline boundary is reached during streaming,"the completed line commits to scrollback with syntax highlighting (not deferred to TurnEnd, not plain text)"
  tui75,"mutable-tail-highlighted",streaming text is in progress with an unterminated tail,the mutable region is rendered,"the tail shows markdown-highlighted content (not plain text)"
  tui76,"cursor-moves-left",the input buffer contains text and the cursor is not at the start,the user presses Left arrow,"the cursor moves left by one character (respecting multi-byte boundaries) and new input inserts at the new position"
  tui77,"code-block-commits-with-highlight",an assistant reply streams a fenced code block containing a blank line between statements,the closing fence arrives during streaming,the complete code block commits as one unit with syntax highlighting (the internal blank line did not split it)
  tui78,"h1-bold-underlined","a level-1 heading is rendered via TestBackend",the heading row cell styles are inspected,the style carries both BOLD and UNDERLINED modifiers
  tui78,"h3-bold-italic","a level-3 heading is rendered via TestBackend",the heading row cell styles are inspected,the style carries both BOLD and ITALIC modifiers
  tui79,"ordered-list-numbers-increment",an assistant reply containing an ordered list (1. a / 2. b / 3. c) is finalized and rendered via TestBackend,the buffer is inspected,"the first item row carries a 1. marker, the second a 2. marker, the third a 3. marker, each colored light_blue"
  tui82,"hard-width-error-on-overflow",a widget returns a StyledLine whose display width exceeds the render width,the engine attempts to render the frame,the engine aborts with a diagnostic (rather than silently wrapping and desyncing the diff)
  tui83,"resize-event-triggers-render",the user resizes the terminal while a turn is streaming,"the crossterm Event::Resize is delivered","a render frame is scheduled at the new dimensions and the content re-flows without losing the streaming tail or the input cursor"
  tui83,"font-zoom-handled",the user changes the terminal font size (changing rows and columns) while the TUI is idle,a render frame occurs,the layout reflows to the new dimensions and no content is lost or corrupted
  tui84,"buffer-length-padding-short-content",content is 2 rows with terminal height=8,do_render sets previous_viewport_top,"previous_viewport_top = max(0, max(8, 2) - 8) = 0 (using bufferLength=8, not bufferLength=2)"
  tui84,"buffer-length-normal",content is 12 rows with terminal height=8,do_render sets previous_viewport_top,"previous_viewport_top = max(0, max(8, 12) - 8) = 4"
  tui84,"no-viewport-top-modification-in-strategies",the Tui struct fields are inspected after a full render and a diff render,previous_viewport_top is checked,"the field is set only by do_render, not mutated inside diff_render or full_render"
  tui84,"viewport-zero-after-clear",content was 15 rows and force_clear triggers a full render with clear of all content,a new frame is rendered with 0 rows,"previous_viewport_top = max(0, max(8, 0) - 8) = 0"
